Export the payloads of a Matroska segment's Info and Chapters elements.

A Matroska file can describe a timeline rather than a plain run of media: an ordered edition plays
its chapters in their own order, a chapter can play a range or a whole edition of another file named
by its SegmentUUID, and segments chain through PrevUUID and NextUUID (RFC 9559, sections 20.2 to
20.4). The demuxer reads one edition as plain chapters and none of the rest, and an AVChapter has no
place for nested chapters, edition flags, skip types or links, so a caller that plays such a file
the way mpv and VLC do has to read those elements itself.

The demuxer now keeps the payload of the segment's first Info element and of its first Chapters
element, the bytes between the element's size and its end exactly as the file holds them, and
exports them as two read-only binary options, "info_payload" and "chapters_payload", on a new
AVClass of the Matroska demuxer. An option is unset when the file has no such element, when its
length is unknown, or when it is larger than 16 MiB, and the element is then parsed as before.

The payload is read back from the IO buffer after the element is parsed, so the parse is untouched.
ffio_ensure_seekback() keeps such a span only for an input that cannot seek, on the reasoning that
one that can seek will serve the bytes again, which over a network is a second request that can
fail an open that worked. The new ffio_ensure_buffered() keeps it on every input, so the export
never asks the input for a byte twice. A Chapters element after the clusters, which only the
SeekHead reaches, is exported the same way.

Applied by BuildFFmpegTask before configure, after 0013, whose context fields it sits beside.
Part of yuroyami/KiteFFmpeg#173.

